#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""apex-oledd - arbitration daemon for the Apex Pro Gen 3 OLED.

One process owns the panel. Sources declare a priority and whether they
currently have anything to say; the highest-priority active source wins the
screen. Without this, every producer would be a separate cron job racing to be
the last writer.

Sources, highest priority first:

    notify  (100)  transient frames pushed over the IPC socket by `apex-oled`
    game     (30)  thermals + swap thrash, while gamemode is active
    lyrics   (20)  now playing + synced lyric line, from the nowplaying daemon
    idle      (0)  RAM/VRAM bars over CPU and GPU rows - always active

Adding one is a subclass with active()/render(); see Source below.

Burn-in: this is an OLED showing largely static content, so the whole frame is
nudged around a small pixel-shift orbit, and the panel blanks when the session
locks. Content is drawn inside a margin so the shift never clips it.

Config lives at ~/.config/apex-oled/config.toml; see DEFAULTS.
"""
